<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#potato">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Potato</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The potato is a starchy tuber native to the Andes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, spread worldwide after the Spanish conquest. As part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columbian-exchange">Columbian exchange</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, it transformed diets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. New World crops helped support the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>'s large population growth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/potato.jpg" alt="Potato" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amédée Masclef · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:234_Solanum_tuberosum_L.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
